      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Digestive System – Meaning and Need"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The human digestive system comprises the alimentary canal along with digestive glands like the salivary glands, liver, and pancreas.",
        "Digestion begins in the mouth and buccal cavity where salivary amylase breaks down complex starches.",
        "The stomach secretes gastric juice containing Hydrochloric Acid (HCl), pepsin, and mucus for protein digestion and microbial defence.",
        "The small intestine serves as the principal site for complete chemical digestion and nutrient absorption via microvilli.",
        "The large intestine mainly reabsorbs water and essential minerals, forming solid waste for elimination."
      ],
      "id": "6x9h9df"
