      "content": "12. Large Intestine – Functions"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Liver is the largest gland in the human body; bile secreted by it contains no digestive enzymes but emulsifies fats.",
        "Hydrochloric acid (HCl) in the stomach activates pepsinogen into pepsin and provides an acidic medium (pH 1.8) for digestion.",
        "Pancreatic juice contains trypsin, amylase, and lipase, functioning effectively in an alkaline environment provided by bile.",
        "Villi and microvilli are specialized finger-like projections in the small intestine that immensely increase surface area for nutrient absorption."
      ],
